{
  "final_report": "- Physical interpretation: eta ≡ (U^{0.5} y)/(nu^{0.5} x^{0.5}) is the Blasius similarity variable: it measures the balance between streamwise advection and transverse viscous diffusion that collapses u/U onto a single profile f(eta) (so u/U = f(eta)). Validation: success.\n- RAG grounding: No exact classical identity is established; closest is Reynolds number Re = U L/nu. Algebraically eta = (y/x)·sqrt(Re_x), so Re_x (inertial/viscous ratio) provides the physical competition motivating this similarity.",
